  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14250845/assets/4ab1cb82bca3650868b7e654cb52d3eb7a0c3101ab4d6a3458485865ae353264.png)\n\nDetermine the lateral surface area for the cube above.",
  "worked_solution": "The lateral surface area ${S}_{L}$ of a cube can be found using the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=4{s}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the side length of the cube.\n\nSubstituting $s=3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}$ into the formula, we get \n\n$$\n{S}_{L}=4(3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm})^{2}=180\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$",
